{"id": "sevt_013qqEn8AdmDkranhfQnyQ8A", "content": [{"text": "**Timeline**\n- The checkout deploy `ccf7a0f` went out at 14:46:05.\n- Checkout p99 was about 70\u201380 ms until 14:45. It jumped to 3006 ms at 14:46 and stayed at 3\u20134.3 s.\n- The other deploys were inventory at 12:20 and cart at 14:18. Neither lines up with the spike.\n\n**Diff**\n- `ccf7a0f` is described as a readability refactor of `build_summary`.\n- It replaced one batched `order_id IN (...)` query with a loop that queries `order_items` once per open order. That is an N+1 query pattern.\n\n**Log**\n- Before 14:46, checkout logs a single `WHERE order_id IN (?)` query per request.\n- The log has 1555 per-row `WHERE order_id = ?` queries. The first query pattern I printed was the batched form at 14:00, and none of the 14:40\u201314:45 queries matched the per-row pattern.\n- I did not check the timestamps of the 1555 per-row queries. I also did not look at per-request query counts or DB pool utilization.\n\n> **Root cause:** `ccf7a0f` \u2014 the \"readability\" refactor of `build_summary` replaced the single batched `order_items` query with one query per order (N+1), which multiplies DB round-trips per checkout request and pushes p99 from about 75 ms to over 3 s.\n\nReverting `ccf7a0f`, or restoring the batched query, should fix it.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T05:45:27.016939Z", "type": "agent.message"}
